WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:20.000
Muscles of Facial Expression: Second Pharyngeal Arch Musculature.

00:00:20.000 --> 00:00:45.000
All muscles of facial expression develop from the mesoderm of the second pharyngeal arch and are innervated by the facial nerve (CN VII).

00:00:45.000 --> 00:01:10.000
Orbicularis oculi surrounds the orbital rim, closing the palpebral fissure; orbicularis oris surrounds the mouth, creating the oral sphincter.

00:01:10.000 --> 00:01:35.000
The buccinator forms the muscular basis of the cheek, pierced by the parotid duct at the level of the upper second molar.

00:01:35.000 --> 00:02:00.000
Clinical Pearl: Lower motor neuron injury to CN VII causes ipsilateral facial paralysis (Bell's palsy) affecting forehead wrinkle and eye closure.
